1788:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    Send the system description string to the host.
1789:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    The system description is used by SystemViewer to identify the
1790:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    current application and handle events accordingly.
1791:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
1792:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *  Parameters
1793:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    sSysDesc - Pointer to the 0-terminated system description string.
1794:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
1795:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *  Additional information
1796:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    One system description string may not exceed SEGGER_SYSVIEW_MAX_STRING_LEN characters.
1797:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
1798:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    The Following items can be described in a system description string.
1799:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    Each item is identified by its identifier, followed by '=' and the value.
1800:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    Items are separated by ','.
1801:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** */
